==== a comma builds a tuple
1, 2
----
(tuple (num "1") (num "2"))

==== tuples are flat, not nested pairs
1, 2, 3
----
(tuple (num "1") (num "2") (num "3"))

==== parens nest a tuple inside a tuple (qna: item 1 of ((1, 2), 3) is 3)
(1, 2), 3
----
(tuple (tuple (num "1") (num "2")) (num "3"))

==== a semicolon builds a collection
1; 2; 3
----
(coll (num "1") (num "2") (num "3"))

==== comma binds tighter than semicolon
1, 2; 3, 4
----
(coll (tuple (num "1") (num "2")) (tuple (num "3") (num "4")))

==== the error fallback binds tighter than a comma
1 | 0, 2 | 0
----
(tuple (bar (num "1") (num "0")) (bar (num "2") (num "0")))

==== the error fallback is looser than an of chain
name of it | "none"
----
(bar (of (ref "name") it) (str "none"))

==== a set literal is a collection under of
set of (2; 78; 80)
----
(of (ref "set") (coll (num "2") (num "78") (num "80")))

==== a tuple is an of operand
(w, b) of c
----
(of (tuple (ref "w") (ref "b")) (ref "c"))

==== a collection of of-chains
(packages "docker-ce" of it; packages "docker" of it)
----
(coll
  (of (ref "packages" (str "docker-ce")) it)
  (of (ref "packages" (str "docker")) it))

==== a trailing comma is an error
1, 2,
----
ERROR line 1 column 6

==== a tuple index is its own node, not a property access
item 0 of (1, 2, 3)
----
(item-of (num "0") (tuple (num "1") (num "2") (num "3")))

==== the plural spelling is the same node, marked plural (qna: `items 1 of ("a","b") | "x"` is `A singular expression is required.`)
items 0 of (1, 2, 3)
----
(items-of (num "0") (tuple (num "1") (num "2") (num "3")))

==== a tuple index too big for an integer is still a tuple index; the checker refuses it (qna: "integer constant was too large" / "not an integer literal", all targets)
item 99999999999999999999 of (1, 2)
----
(item-of (num "99999999999999999999") (tuple (num "1") (num "2")))

==== a string tuple index is an error, not a property (qna: item "foo" of folder is "tuple index which was not an integer literal", all targets)
item "foo" of folder "c:\temp"
----
ERROR line 1 column 6

==== a computed tuple index is an error too (qna: item (0+1) of (1,2) is "not an integer literal")
item (0+1) of (1, 2)
----
ERROR line 1 column 6

==== a parenthesized integer literal is still a tuple index (qna: item (1) of (1,2) is 2)
item (1) of (1, 2)
----
(item-of (num "1") (tuple (num "1") (num "2")))

==== the plural `items` is a property too, not aggregation
items of folder "c:\temp"
----
(of (ref "items") (ref "folder" (str "c:\\temp")))

==== a decimal-point index is not writable -- there is no such numeral syntax
item 1.5 of (1, 2)
----
ERROR line 1 column 7

==== the error fallback is its own node, not a binary operator
size of file "c:\nope.txt" | 42
----
(bar (of (ref "size") (ref "file" (str "c:\\nope.txt"))) (num "42"))
